A||||3||87GT||Brake Upgrade Question||||5||
Z||000000||87GT||02-19-2001||09:15 PM||||I just recently got the Fiero Store brake upgrade system for the front and rear brakes on my fiero.  I installed the vented rotor package and new calipers in the front as usual and the cross drilled rotors in the rear.  The problem is, I still have a mushy pedal when I apply the brakes.. I can stand on the pedal and it wont lock up the brakes at all.  The car has a tendancy to pull to the left too.  It acts really squirrely.  I am thinking it may do this becuase of my worn out cradle bushings which are going to be replaced later this week.. But, the mushy pedal and sub par braking is what has got me very aggravated.  Any suggestions will be appreciated.  Thanks.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||02-19-2001||09:31 PM||||bleed it again. This time jack the back of the car up or point it down hill untill you get the nose of the master cyl level.<P>If that doesn't work then you may have to bench bleed the MC again. then repeat the above.<P>If that still doesn't solve it then you have other problems. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 02-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||BN Boomer||02-19-2001||10:04 PM||||Does it pull to the left all of the time or just when you apply the brakes? Did it do this before the conversion? If it pulls to the left all of the time, it could be a stuck or sticking caliper. If only when braking, then one side isn't working properly or at all. The mushiness and "sub-par" braking are practically garuanteed to be the result of air in the brake fluid. I'd bleed it again before any further diagnosis. <P>I know it's not a Fiero and evryone here is tired of seeing pics of my Suburban, but here is a tool that I find invaluable in bleeding brakes. It's a Might-Vac brake bleeder, it works by creating vacuum to draw the bubbles out of the brake fluid. It's truly wonderful. Here I'm using it to bleed the brakes on the 'burb after replacing the caliper and brake hose.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/boomers_fiero_files/mvc-002f.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||02-20-2001||12:07 AM||||It's a mity-vac!  Those things rule, I bought one a couple months ago.  Work great for bleeding brakes, can also use them as a vacuum gauge, tester, etc, etc... ||||reg||1
